# Testing — colocated vitest, AAA

## Context

Tests live next to the code they cover (e.g. `app/src/reducer.test.ts`,
`app/src/store.test.ts`) and run via **vitest**, not Jest or Mocha. `cd app &&
npm test` must stay green.

## Rule

- New tests are colocated: `app/src/<name>.ts` → `app/src/<name>.test.ts`
  (or under `app/src/lib/` for lib code).
- Use vitest's `describe`/`it`/`expect` — no other test runner.
- Follow **Arrange-Act-Assert**: set up state/action, dispatch or call the
  function under test, assert the result. Keep each test focused on one
  behavior.
- Any new `Action` variant or reducer case gets at least one test. Any new
  `app/src/lib/text.ts` behavior gets a test too.
- Never delete or weaken an existing test to make it pass; fix the code or
  ask first.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm test` exits 0.
2. Every new/changed source file under `app/src` has a corresponding
   `*.test.ts` change or addition alongside it.
3. `grep -rn "describe\|it(" app/src/**/*.test.ts` shows AAA-shaped tests
   (setup, action, assertion) rather than one giant assertion blob.
